The allocation is fair according to the Nash bargaining solution as it maximises the product of individual utilities. The Nash bargaining solution is a widely accepted solution concept in game theory for reaching an agreement when multiple parties with different preferences have to reach a consensus. In this case, the Nash bargaining solution would be to allocate Good A to Person 2, Good B to Person 1, and discard Good C, as this would give the largest product of utilities for the two individuals. The utility for Person 1 would be 46 and the utility for Person 2 would be 47. The product of utilities would be 46 * 47 = 2162.

